The files in Sources/UsageCore/Upstream and the selected ClaudeSubscriptionTests
derive from AIUsage. Modifications include removing proxy/server and OAuth refresh
code, adding memory-only read-only quota fetches, isolating storage paths, extracting
shared data types, and extending the streaming JSON projection for Codex usage.
The QuotaBar projection skips unused conversation and tool metadata while preserving
numeric usage fields, and daily aggregation avoids per-event string formatting.
New application UI, scheduling, keychain integration, and local usage aggregation
are provided as part of this independent lightweight adaptation.
The activity cards in Sources/QuotaBar/ActivityView.swift adapt the upstream
DashboardView+Heatmap.swift layout, calendar grid, and tooltip presentation.
Colors and provider symbols use QuotaBar's shared application theme.
CodexLogo.png, ClaudeLogo.svg, and GeminiLogo.png are the unmodified provider
logos from the upstream assets.
The data adapter uses QuotaBar's bounded local token reports without proxy ledgers.
Codex browser sign-in now delegates to the locally installed official Codex CLI
in an isolated temporary home. App-owned OAuth refresh and rotation persistence
are implemented separately, using the public Codex client parameters also present
in the upstream Codex provider. Imported CLI files remain read-only.

No CLIProxyAPI, Sparkle, browser runtime, or upstream sponsor assets are bundled.
